   252	branch except B avoids ṽ, hence has determinant ⩾ 1 by [4], Lemma 4.  For B
   253	itself, (F2) leaves exactly two possibilities: B is a connected component of
   254	F⁻¹(U_q), whence `det B = 1` by (F1); or B is the linear branch, whence
   255	`det B > 0`.  Either way `det B ⩾ 1`, so `det Q₃ ⩾ 1 > 0`.
   256	
   257	**(4) The inequality (2.13) with i = 1.**  By (1)–(3),
   258	`det(q̃g̃₁) = 1 ⩽ (det δ(q̃g̃₁))²·det Q₃`, since the right-hand side is a
   259	product of positive integers.
   260	
   261	With Lemma DET-LINF supplying `det L̃∞ ⩽ 0`, Lemma 2.12 applies and yields
   262	ṽ ∈ Q₁ ∪ Q₂.  But ṽ ∈ B ⊆ Q₃, and Q₁, Q₂, Q₃ are pairwise disjoint.
   263	Contradiction. ∎
   264	
