   282	branches at s̃_j other than the two path branches are, by (F2), the remaining
   283	components of F⁻¹(U_{s_j}) (determinant 1 by (F1)) together with the linear
   284	branch R̃_{s̃_j}.  Induct on j.  For j = 1 there is no nodal vertex strictly
   285	between g̃₁ and s̃₁, so `δ(s̃₁g̃₁) = ∅` and `det δ(s̃₁g̃₁) = 1`; Lemma 2.3
