   327	Proposition 3.4 c) any linear chain at s̃ has degree n(s̃); the chain towards
   328	g̃₂ has degree 2 by Lemma 1.5, so n(s̃) = 2; Definition 3.2 b) then gives
   329	`det(s̃g̃₂) = (n(s̃)·n(g̃₂)/Deg)·det R_s = (2·2/2)·1 = 2`, using
