xmodel/b0-all-n-eta-criticality-sol56-20260831.md:411:The \(\mu\ge2\) component is required by branch-locus nonemptiness (**B0:190--211**), and \(\mu=N-1\) is excluded by promoted Corollary 3.8 (**Coord:46--48**). Different target components have different normalization maps. Moreover H2 strictness does not supply a correction on the component seen by a trivial dicritical. Thus the common-eta argument is only componentwise and need not meet any correction.
